Restore RSA key transport for TLS 1.2 (TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256,
TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384), which Mbed TLS 4.0 removed.

Why: some old servers (www.fsf.org) offer no key exchange with forward
secrecy that Aura has. Aura offers these two suites after every other
suite, and only while its security.legacy_tls preference is on
(src/net/tls.c, au_tls_allow_legacy_kex).

What: the option AURA_MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_RSA (set in
third_party/mbedtls-config) adds the key exchange type, the two suites,
the client's ClientKeyExchange (a 48-byte premaster secret encrypted to
the server certificate's RSA key with PKCS#1 v1.5, through PSA), the
keyEncipherment key usage check, and, for the tests' server only
(MBEDTLS_SSL_SRV_C), the server's side with the countermeasure to
Bleichenbacher's attack. The client and server code follow
ssl_write_encrypted_pms and ssl_parse_encrypted_pms of Mbed TLS 3.6
(same licence). Without the option the library is unchanged.

To drop it: delete this file, remove AURA_MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_RSA and
PSA_WANT_ALG_RSA_PKCS1V15_CRYPT from third_party/mbedtls-config, remove
suites_legacy and au_tls_allow_legacy_kex from src/net/tls.c and the
rsa_kex option from tests/net/fakenet.c, and run apply.sh.

